    "q-13822": {
      "dom_id": "step-q13822",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{1}{3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{3x}\\cdot 3=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
