    "q-31394": {
      "dom_id": "step-q31394",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "$\\int \\frac{{log}_{5}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "Let $u={log}_{5}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{5}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {log}_{5}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\int u\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\int u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{5}^{2}⁡x}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-31394-a",
